d squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =2\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{2} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{4} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ {y}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+{y}^{2}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186152804 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "3754726d-eb07-5177-bde1-2e130a929394" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+\\frac{(y-1)^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345826} {:answer/id #uuid "41933836-9e91-5567-ae93-cdca54f3119c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{16}+(y+1)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345910} {:answer/id #uuid "634f6c56-30af-534a-9acf-909105673bdf" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346215} {:answer/id #uuid "85b84dc3-77f6-5317-bc63-cba7718f74d5" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-1)^{2}}{4}+(y+1)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346513} {:answer/id #uuid "97060e97-47b0-5626-85ea-a37318a871be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+(y-1)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346673}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "97060e97-47b0-5626-85ea-a37318a871be" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+(y-1)^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346673} :answer-field/id #uuid "16df9bb4-f58f-542f-8d1a-7a5f96d7b152" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186347649}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "ddcf2b55-d913-5f98-8f2e-d38863acbf2e" :question/math-academy-id "q-79375" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1,\\,y=\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -1 \\\\ \\frac{x+1}{4} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +1 \\\\ y-1 & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ (y-1)^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+(y-1)^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{16}+(y-1)^{2}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241170 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "1e2739d8-8263-5715-80a0-b