peratorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{4} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{4}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{16}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241171 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "430731d8-2746-561b-9932-67b216b9fe6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238637} {:answer/id #uuid "6d5367ef-504b-5ba3-a55b-c4c01e11de99" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}-9{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238996} {:answer/id #uuid "e04c2016-5bb4-58d5-b9d6-a2cd96a09d37" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "9{x}^{2}+4{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240017} {:answer/id #uuid "e0b0efb3-ded6-535b-9129-9f1e0979660f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{1}{9}{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240025} {:answer/id #uuid "e0f34c9d-d585-551d-ad3a-8864f684d38c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{x}^{2}-\\frac{1}{9}{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240028}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "430731d8-2746-561b-9932-67b216b9fe6e" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238637} :answer-field/id #uuid "e50ff31d-bfd9-5fd4-b0bd-dcf00ea22347" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240730}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "6677d4ff-0012-5e92-83bc-c53813937d2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-106406" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4{x}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 3y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 9{y}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n4{x}^{2}+9{y}^{2}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241172 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "29c85e08-cf6a-5307-80f4-ce01ca0ebcac" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238422} {:answer/id #uuid "45c84b8d-f295-5003-a523-bb16c6bcf8f2" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}-\\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238658} {:answer/id #uuid "689800b2-34c6-5ad7-a7b0-9045f353fb27" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}{x}^{2}+\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238964} {:answer/id #uuid "ae4de9d6-48b4-5098-a575-119212df9e4a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{4}{9}{x}^{2}-\\frac{9}{4}{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239570} {:answer/id #uuid "c35b39d0-2b50-56f0-b092-5a399f164c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239778}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "c35b39d0-2b50-56f0-b092-5a399f164c51" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239778} :answer-field/id #uuid "45dde714-85df-57b8-888c-f62cc7cc39a3" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240450}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9b47425b-d1be-54fd-a4d5-ddff6578df69" :question/math-academy-id "q-106407" :question/problem "Find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{2}{3}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{3}{2}x & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{3}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{2}{3}y & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{4}{x}^{2}+\\frac{4}{9}{y}^{2}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186241173 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0363f299-ebce-5cd3-a3d9-6edbee6ef1d1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{(x-2)}^{2}+\\frac{1}{4}{(y-3)}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238110} {:answer/id #uuid "09798478-efa7-5adb-b8d0-a50d61788683" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{(x-2)}^{2}-4{(y-3)}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238149} {:answer/id #uuid "117cba79-f965-5374-92ac-bc6e684c94b1" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{(x-3)}^{2}+4{(y-2)}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186238201} {:answer/id #uuid "ae1fc9c6-aa5a-5af7-8fe4-228cbf131588" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{1}{4}{(x-2)}^{2}-\\frac{1}{4}{(y-3)}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239567} {:answer/id #uuid "d42beaa6-50c5-5dd1-9084-6b775db8f4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{(x-2)}^{2}+4{(y-3)}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239919}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "d42beaa6-50c5-5dd1-9084-6b775db8f4aa" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "4{(x-2)}^{2}+4{(y-3)}^{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186239919} :answer-field/id #uuid "57eda148-ff6d-5235-8674-30b291d678a9" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186240493}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "f6811d7d-6469-50eb-bfd3-5c7960859395" :question/math-academy-id "q-106408" :question/problem "Calculate the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2,\\,y=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +2 \\\\ x-2 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2(x-2) & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4{(x-2)}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +3 \\\\ y-3 & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 2(y-3) & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ 4{(y-3)}^{2} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{(x-2)}^{2}+4{(y-3)}^{2} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n4{(x-2)}^{2}+4{(y-3)}^{2}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186243934 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "365c4773-e368-5e9e-b8d3-09d97f8cf201" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186241658} {:answer/id #uuid "6115395b-4dd0-5476-84c1-62a064355b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242054} {:answer/id #uuid "718e50be-5a17-5e14-88c8-db7be4da154a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242189} {:answer/id #uuid "a8ffe555-2803-571a-a13e-b08b1c573270" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242663} {:answer/id #uuid "db656494-d26d-54fd-a2be-e62b928fc054" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{3}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{5}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243129}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "6115395b-4dd0-5476-84c1-62a064355b01" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186242054} :answer-field/id #uuid "2a7931ea-4640-57b6-8a13-7f713b36ad36" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186243514}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "00eda352-d2e8-5490-8b6e-f1ece02f57de" :question/math-academy-id "q-106715" :question/problem "Determine the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =3\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{3} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{9} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{5} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186275403 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d8f1b2b-173b-5b92-b859-1ec4e15fc869" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272505} {:answer/id #uuid "2e0ec060-43c6-5507-a4b4-71bf27bfdb41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272798} {:answer/id #uuid "3d24278c-1604-5a0e-92c8-91b968fed491" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{5}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{3}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272912} {:answer/id #uuid "6793780e-4123-58f7-8dac-1bc0e63caa25" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273279} {:answer/id #uuid "7c9ffd0c-5022-5c83-b63e-3c3cbf9ed38c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{9}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{25}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186273455}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2e0ec060-43c6-5507-a4b4-71bf27bfdb41" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186272798} :answer-field/id #uuid "30cc30d9-eb2f-5ad6-9d67-21da1b5948c8" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186274721}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "3ccbcc93-cb2d-5c7d-ae5c-a7e728fdad2b" :question/math-academy-id "q-15792" :question/problem "Determine the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =5\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{5} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{5}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{25} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{3} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{3}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{25}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{9}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186278183 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "044aa764-a402-587b-9d4c-b41637dfa030" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186275516} {:answer/id #uuid "8324a325-41e1-54bc-8b74-1c52b4799e1a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186276657} {:answer/id #uuid "c4127d31-6dc3-521f-8215-809b40a67775" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{6}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{2}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277220} {:answer/id #uuid "d2c6cd3a-dd09-5f85-a646-0e12c483a833" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{4}-\\frac{{y}^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277337} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c3aad5-29e3-5b96-b737-92612b8b8109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277461}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "e2c3aad5-29e3-5b96-b737-92612b8b8109" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277461} :answer-field/id #uuid "17b8f849-09df-52e8-a517-f7b406de368f" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186277767}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "48febb37-71be-5629-b005-ff375ac1902f" :question/math-academy-id "q-15843" :question/problem "Determine the Cartesian equation of the ellipse\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{6} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{36} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{2} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{2}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n \nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{36}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{4}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302350 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "2506dc2c-9a48-5ddf-a190-045af9bb3db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300138}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "2506dc2c-9a48-5ddf-a190-045af9bb3db0" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{28}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300138} :answer-field/id #uuid "e51629cd-762c-5f50-ba6f-6feeb02fa23d" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301952}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "bcd20c00-207d-5776-ad99-e9ea0fea55dc" :question/math-academy-id "q-327798" :question/problem "The Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3,\\,y=2\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -5,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta +3 \\\\ \\frac{x-3}{6} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{{6}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{36} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =2\\sqrt{7}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta -5 \\\\ \\frac{y+5}{2\\sqrt{7}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{(2\\sqrt{7})^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{28} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{28} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-3)^{2}}{36}+\\frac{(y+5)^{2}}{28}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302351 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "7bc28628-0500-5a4e-b7c4-aab08e1def7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{100}+\\frac{(y-12)^{2}}{99}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300578}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "7bc28628-0500-5a4e-b7c4-aab08e1def7c" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{100}+\\frac{(y-12)^{2}}{99}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300578} :answer-field/id #uuid "15b576c6-b6ea-547c-b701-c6162e1d6269" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301296}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "cf7a561b-81b3-5465-9ed7-22d55b60ba48" :question/math-academy-id "q-327803" :question/problem "The Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4,\\,y=3\\sqrt{11}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +12,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter  $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =10\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta -4 \\\\ \\frac{x+4}{10} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{{10}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{100} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =3\\sqrt{11}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta +12 \\\\ \\frac{y-12}{3\\sqrt{11}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(y-12)^{2}}{(3\\sqrt{11})^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{(y-12)^{2}}{99} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{100}+\\frac{(y-12)^{2}}{99} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x+4)^{2}}{100}+\\frac{(y-12)^{2}}{99}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302352 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "78ec0879-40ef-5eca-bcab-024dcd2d2ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{96}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300557}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "78ec0879-40ef-5eca-bcab-024dcd2d2ae8" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{96}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300557} :answer-field/id #uuid "9e7318c6-8514-5dcc-b694-eb9615ec63ae" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301737}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "42002e7f-0b06-57fa-9bb9-6d321bc37cf7" :question/math-academy-id "q-327808" :question/problem "The Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=4\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=5\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =4\\sqrt{6}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{4\\sqrt{6}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(4\\sqrt{6})^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{96} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =5\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{5\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(5\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{50} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{96}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{96}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{50}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302353 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "ab159e0e-467d-5f21-8fde-88f54619f27f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{48}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300821}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ab159e0e-467d-5f21-8fde-88f54619f27f" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{48}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300821} :answer-field/id #uuid "28d87d77-faf2-51e3-8007-0a1b765c8eff" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301356}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c43bad9-0cfd-52b5-8797-68675d788468" :question/math-academy-id "q-327809" :question/problem "The Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$ We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =9\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{9} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{{9}^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{81} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =4\\sqrt{3}\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{4\\sqrt{3}} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{(4\\sqrt{3})^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{48} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{48}={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{81}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{48}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186302354 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "40ab42d7-89d3-5227-b9a9-2d4a46ac75dc" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{{x}^{2}}{72}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{121}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186300280} {:answer/id #uuid "611e2833-ce93-5c10-9e5b-40b95d3ca49a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{72}+\\frac{y^2}{121}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540693}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "611e2833-ce93-5c10-9e5b-40b95d3ca49a" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^2}{72}+\\frac{y^2}{121}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186540693} :answer-field/id #uuid "2cdeb47f-480e-5ca4-a46f-7f342cc63ce7" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186301369}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "9e4592b8-c042-55bc-b24f-4355e15f5f7f" :question/math-academy-id "q-327811" :question/problem "The Cartesian equation of the ellipse defined by the parametric equations\n\n$$\nx=6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta ,\\,y=11\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta ,\\,0\\le \\theta <2\\pi .\n$$\n\nis given by\n\n{{field-1}}\n$=1.$" :question/worked-solution "To find the Cartesian equation of the ellipse, we need to eliminate the parameter $\\theta .$  We can do this using the Pythagorean theorem.\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta $ term in the $x$-equation and squaring, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =6\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{x}{6\\sqrt{2}} & =\\operatorname{cos}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{(6\\sqrt{2})^{2}} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{x}^{2}}{72} & ={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBy isolating the $\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta $ term in the $y$-equation and squaring, we obtain\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y & =11\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{y}{11} & =\\operatorname{sin}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{{11}^{2}} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta  \\\\ \\frac{{y}^{2}}{121} & ={sin}^{2}⁡\\theta .\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAdding the two equations and using ${cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1,$ we get\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{72}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{121}={cos}^{2}⁡\\theta +{sin}^{2}⁡\\theta =1.\n$$\n\nSo, the Cartesian equation of the ellipse is\n\n$$\n\\frac{{x}^{2}}{72}+\\frac{{y}^{2}}{121}=1.\n$$"} {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186348219 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:knowledge-point/id #uuid "6e75170b-1e28-52c1-b0ab-f50ffde6c262" :knowledge-point/title "The Cartesian Equation of an Ellipse"}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0ad1b940-29ef-5bb3-ab76-b9022d36ef57" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x-5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186345436} {:answer/id #uuid "5bab3d83-01ac-56d9-87c7-89af73d69a22" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{6}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{36}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346134} {:answer/id #uuid "7b0ebee1-e81a-5755-a697-cbac27922e86" :answer/type {:db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{(x+5)^{2}}{9}+\\frac{(y+2)^{2}}{18}=1" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186346426} {:answer/id #uuid "7d3731bc-0af6-503e-8640-17df